6), which could help in creating additional melds for a winning hand.  \nReason: By discarding T7, the player retains T4 and T5, which are critical for forming a Chow if T6 is drawn. This strategy aligns with the goal of building more melds, particularly in the T suit, to reach a winning hand with sufficient points.  \nAnswer: Play T7"}
